The first code statement attempts to free networks without ensuring that all references to these networks are cleared, which can lead to dangling pointers if any part of the code still tries to access these freed networks. The second code statement frees links without properly managing their references, which can also lead to invalid memory access if a link is still being referenced elsewhere in the code.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
while ((network = m->networks))
    network_free(network);
```
```c
while ((link = hashmap_steal_first(m->links))) {
